Subject: host credentials: read the keyring secret from CINDY_HOST_CREDENTIAL_KEY_FILE

Why: on Linux the Host derives its credential key from Secret Service via
secret-tool. Headless servers, containers and NAS apps (fnOS) have none, so
the runtime stops with CREDENTIAL_STORE_UNAVAILABLE ("Unlock the system
keyring"). When the variable is set, createCredentialStore reads the keyring
secret from that owner-only file and derives the key with the same
deriveLinuxOsCryptKey, so records stay OSCrypt v11. Missing, empty or
group/world-accessible files fail; there is no keyring or plaintext fallback.
Unset keeps today's behavior.
Upstream: not yet proposed. Draft issue: docs/upstream/credential-key-file/issue.md
Remove when: upstream Host can take its Linux credential key from a file (or
another non-Secret-Service source) without this patch.

diff --git a/apps/host/src/credentials/store.mjs b/apps/host/src/credentials/store.mjs
index 5cac37e6..74e66011 100644
--- a/apps/host/src/credentials/store.mjs
+++ b/apps/host/src/credentials/store.mjs
@@ -32,6 +32,25 @@ export class SafeStorageUnavailableError extends Error {
  * @property {(key: string) => void} remove
  */
 
+/**
+ * Headless Linux (servers, containers, NAS apps) has no Secret Service. The
+ * operator can instead put the keyring secret in an owner-only file named by
+ * CINDY_HOST_CREDENTIAL_KEY_FILE. The key derivation is unchanged, so records
+ * stay v11 and a secret exported from a keyring still decrypts them. A bad file
+ * is fatal: never fall back to the keyring or to plaintext.
+ */
+function readCredentialKeyFile(file) {
+  let secret;
+  try {
+    if (fs.statSync(file).mode & 0o077) throw new Error('accessible by group or others; chmod 600 it');
+    secret = fs.readFileSync(file, 'utf8').replace(/\r?\n$/, '');
+  } catch (error) {
+    throw new SafeStorageUnavailableError(`Cannot use CINDY_HOST_CREDENTIAL_KEY_FILE ${file}: ${error.message}`);
+  }
+  if (!secret) throw new SafeStorageUnavailableError(`CINDY_HOST_CREDENTIAL_KEY_FILE ${file} is empty`);
+  return secret;
+}
+
 /**
